{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtQ57dgzK5G3BoTqWUnK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`CODEX_API_KEY` is not set here, so Codex logs in from `~/.codex/auth.json`. That means the sandboxed lane needs its own `~/.codex` reachable, the same way kimi opens `~/.kimi-code`. Copying `auth.json` into `/tmp` would be worse, since the agent's shell could read it from there.\n\nPlan:\n- Make the profile's state-dir allowance a parameter, `STATE`, instead of a hardcoded `.kimi-code`. Each lane then opens only its own state dir, so kimi doesn't gain access to `~/.codex`.\n- Add a `codex-sandboxed` lane that runs the same `codex exec` call under `sandbox-exec`, with `-o` pointing at a `/tmp` scratch folder that gets copied out afterward.\n\nI'll read the files before editing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3311,"cache_read_input_tokens":37643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3311},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d1964f0-c55b-4297-ad9e-39fd1a6b3b49","uuid":"88c374e6-15c9-4573-a674-855c54f63482","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:43:08.824Z","request_id":"req_011CgtQ57Ukeo5wjb6jP2vNr"}
